# scripts/.maintainer-leak-allowlist — D5 (DC14 item 4: full-line form)
# glob<TAB>rule-id|*<TAB>required-substring<TAB>reason
# An entry suppresses matching hits of either class (FAIL or WARN). It is
# stale, and a FAIL, only if it matches no hit of any class. The substring
# column is the EXACT, stripped, full source line the entry allows -- not
# an arbitrary substring -- so one entry can't accidentally cover a second,
# unrelated line that happens to share a shorter fragment. A file with
# multiple distinct allowed lines gets one entry per line. The empty
# substring is permitted only for the two scrubber migrations below, which
# intentionally blanket-suppress their whole file.
